# Accepted Trivy exceptions for rotate-aws-backups image.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-10-29
# Scope: Trivy gating scan only (HIGH/CRITICAL, ignore-unfixed)
#
# msgpack 1.1.2, urllib3 2.7.0, and setuptools 70.3.0 findings below are
# pip's own internally vendored dependency copies (pip/_vendor/*), bundled
# inside the pip wheel embedded in CPython's ensurepip/_bundled --
# unrelated to this project's own urllib3>=2.7.0 and setuptools>=84.0.0
# floors in requirements.txt (both already current; the standalone
# urllib3 install resolves to 2.8.0, confirmed inside the built image).
# Confirmed pip 26.2.2 is the latest PyPI release and pypa/pip's
# main-branch vendor.txt still pins setuptools==70.3.0 and urllib3==2.7.0;
# the 26.2.2 release also still vendors msgpack==1.1.2 (main's vendor.txt
# has moved to 1.2.3, but no pip release has shipped it yet). None of the
# three is independently upgradable from this Dockerfile. Re-review when
# pip cuts its next release.
